ent-safe"><strong>Equivalent practice 1</strong><p>Explain how changing receptor occupancy can alter response.</p><span class="status">Same objective · distinct formulation</span></div><div class="item-card student-safe"><strong>Equivalent practice 2</strong><p>Compare hypothetical dose-response curves for potency versus efficacy.</p><span class="status">Same difficulty · distinct scenario</span></div><div class="item-card student-safe"><strong>Equivalent practice 3</strong><p>Apply the pharmacodynamic principle to a new scenario and justify the reasoning.</p><span class="status">Transfer learning · no secure-item access</span></div>`}document.querySelectorAll('[data-edu-mode]').forEach(b=>b.onclick=()=>{const m=b.dataset.eduMode;tp.style.display=m==='teacher'?'block':'none';sp.style.display=m==='student'?'block':'none';if(m==='student')student()});const g=document.getElementById('generateSecureAssessment');if(g)g.onclick=()=>{const sub=document.getElementById('assessSubject').value||'Course',d=document.getElementById('assessDifficulty').value;document.getElementById('teacherSecureItems').innerHTML=`<div class="secure-banner"><strong>Instructor-only assessment generated.</strong> Exact items, keys and metadata stay behind instructor authorization.</div><div class="item-card teacher-secure"><strong>Secure item 1</strong><p>${sub}: mechanism-focused item aligned to the first competency.</p><span class="status">Instructor only</span></div><div class="item-card teacher-secure"><strong>Secure item 2</strong><p>${sub}: application item at ${d} depth.</p><span class="status">Instructor only</span></div><div class="item-card teacher-secure"><strong>Secure item 3</strong><p>${sub}: interpretation item using a distinct scenario.</p><span class="status">Instructor only</span></div>`;student()}})();</script>
